@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+---
+type: decision
+status: active
+updated: 2026-11-03
+sources: [.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md, .harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md, 2432c79, ff63170, 2848bef, 0005, 0010, 0011]
+verified_by: tests/gate.test.sh, tests/gate-denied.list
+---
+# 0012: Gate shrink (prune step 5): keep the gate, pin the policy
+
+**Context.** 0005 consequence 4b wanted a ≤50-line gate or none ("permissions rules + small gate"). The analyst inventory (`.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md` §2-3, 552 lines then) replayed 881 conductor Bash calls through the gate: 754 allowed, 127 denied (106 of those from two ungated daemon-env sessions). Used: harness, cat/ls under `.harness`/`docs`, `git log|status|diff --stat|branch`, `gh pr create|merge|view|edit|list|comment|checks`, `herdr pane current|get`. Never used: `git show --stat`, `herdr status|pane list|layout|workspace|tab`, `gh issue|run|repo|auth|browse|pr status`, jq as a pipe consumer; pipes 0 allowed, chaining 44 (5.8%). The B′ spike (native subagents instead of the harness runner) was rejected on 2026-11-03 (`.harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md`): subagents die when the conductor exits ("1 local agent couldn't be moved and was stopped"), so the headless runner and the gate stay.
+
+**Decision.**
+- Trim as planned in the analyst's §6, over steps already merged: (g) gate keys on `agent_type`, (a) single-command scanner (`jq`, `split_segments`, `2>&1` gone), `tests/gate-denied.list` regression list. Steps (b)(c)(d) were already in effect when this step started: gh only `pr create|view|list|checks|comment|edit|merge`, `git branch` by regex (list-only), herdr `pane get|current`, no Agent/Workflow/Monitor/NotebookEdit/`mcp__filesystem__*` cases (conductor.md `disallowedTools` covers the first four; no filesystem MCP is configured), MATCHER `Edit|Write|Read|Grep|Glob|Bash`. This step verified that, pinned every "You may run directly" form with a gate test, and changed nothing in policy.
+- (e) done in ff63170: deny messages, `BASH_ALLOW`, `GH_ALLOW`, `GIT_DENY` sit in one labelled block at the top of the gate; the code below only applies them.
+- `--via` removed (2432c79): a no-op since step 4, now an unknown option (exit 1, no run).
+- Kept: the path helpers (`rel`, `physrel`, `physical`, raw-stream check, ~109 lines) and the Bash allowlist. They are the symlink and `.harness/log/*.jsonl` protection; a 50-line gate cannot keep them.
+- Option (f), permissions rules instead of the gate, rejected: user-scope `permissions` bind workers too (same settings file), deny beats allow so "deny Read except `.harness`/`docs`" cannot be written, and Bash patterns are fragile. Only tool-name denies are expressible, and `disallowedTools` already does those.
+
+**Status.** Active. Supersedes the 4b consequence of 0005. Gate 552 → 522 lines (analyst baseline to now, banner included).
+
+**Consequences.** The gate is still the one place that scopes reads and writes; changing what the conductor may run means editing the policy block and `claude/agents/conductor.md` together, plus a test. A filesystem MCP server added later is ungated unless `mcp__filesystem` is added to `disallowedTools` (prefix support unverified). The gate is live-symlinked: `bash -n` and `tests/gate.test.sh` before every save, new inode (see Live gate edit).
